    <DataNode elementId="AT4G25100-MONOMER" textLabel="Superoxide dismutase [Fe] 1, chloroplastic" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="AT4G25100.1" dataSource="TAIR gene name" />
      <Graphics centerX="450" centerY="475" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">NIL The cDNA encoding the iron-dependent superoxide dismutase (SOD) FSD1 has been isolated from &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt;. FSD1 belongs to a small gene family in Arabidopsis with at least three iron-dependent SOD&apos;s. Its molecular function could be confirmed by functional complementation of a mutant &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt; |CITS: [2263641]|. The FSD1 gene was the only SOD that was expressed due to diurnal oscillation and appears to be under circadian control accumulating in rosette leaves under standard 16-h-photoperiod growth conditions. It was discussed that FSD1 among other plastitic SOD&apos;s provides adaptation towards a number of different oxidative stresses and responds to diurnal-light-mediated reactive oxygen species (ROS) fluctuations |CITS: [9765550]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT4G25100-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT4G25100.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pid" value="AAA32791" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="FE SUPEROXIDE DISMUTASE 1" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-13451" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT4G25100.1" />
      <Property key="FunctionalAssignmentStatus" value=":PROBABLE-ENZYME" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT4G25100" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <Property key="MolecularWeightExp" value="23." />
      <Property key="MolecularWeightKd" value="23." />
