    <DataNode elementId="AT5G51100-MONOMER" textLabel="Superoxide dismutase [Fe] 2, chloroplastic" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="O04879" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="555" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">NIL The cDNA encoding the iron-dependent superoxide dismutase (SOD) FSD2 has been isolated from &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt;. FSD2 belongs to a small gene family in Arabidopsis with at least three iron-dependent SOD&apos;s. The FSD2 gene was expressed in rosette leaves of Arabidopsis and has been discussed to contribute to the adaptation of transient, photoproduced reactive oxygen species (ROS) fluctuations |CITS: [9765550]|.</Comment>
